Delivered on branch fix/8nec-post-commit-hook, head 301580800 (2 commits: 25032dc8f + guard allowlist 301580800). Not merged; awaiting review/landing.

WHAT CHANGED — bead options A + B, both implemented:
A. The subject is never a note source. scripts/bump-version.mjs gains `--hook` mode: the note comes from `--user-note` only. scripts/git-hooks/post-commit now reads the note from a `Release-note: <what the user gets>` line in the commit body, or CAP_USER_NOTE in the environment; with neither, it bumps nothing and writes no entry (and prints the interface).
B. One bump per branch. Hook mode compares the working version with `git show origin/main:extension/manifest.json`; when they differ the branch already carries the bump (or is behind main) and nothing is written, with the reason named in the output.
AGENTS.md documents the author interface next to the hook install instructions.

Manual path unchanged: `node scripts/bump-version.mjs patch --user-note "<copy>"` still bumps/relabels explicitly; `--message` inference remains only for non-hook manual use so existing sanitize tests are untouched.

EVIDENCE — tests/post-commit-hook.test.ts (new, 6 tests) installs the REFERENCE hook in a scratch git repository and makes real commits:
- plain user-facing subject, no trailer → no version consumed, no entry, loud notice (the false-positive the bead recorded: "delete the journal guess instead of guarding");
- bookkeeping subject → no bump;
- jargon subject `fix(harness): rework the bridge transport` + plain trailer → bumps to the trailer copy, HEAD amended with the bumped surfaces (the false-negative the bead recorded);
- CAP_USER_NOTE with no trailer → bumps;
- second trailer on the same branch → no second bump, exactly one 1.2.4 entry, second note not published;
- branch behind origin/main → refuses to consume a version, names origin/main's version.

GATES: `npm run test:file -- tests/post-commit-hook.test.ts` 6/6; `npm run test:changed` (failed closed to the full suite) after the guard fix; production rebuild after the last commit; `npm test` 4509 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored (exit 0). The durable-root guard initially flagged the new test's tmpdir fixture; it is now in the ephemeral-fixtures allowance list (patch 301580800).

INSTALL NOTE (operational, coordinator call): the machine-local .git/hooks/post-commit still holds the old policy — hooks are shared by every worktree, so switching it changes bump behaviour for every lane mid-flight. Install when the fleet should switch: cp scripts/git-hooks/post-commit .git/hooks/post-commit && chmod +x .git/hooks/post-commit. Until then the reference hook (and its tests) carry the new policy.

description:
Found while verifying the cthe landing (53e28546) on merged main.

scripts/cthe-npt-directory-evidence.ts ends with an unguarded teardown:

    } finally {
      proc.kill("SIGKILL");
      server.kill("SIGKILL");
    }
    console.log(`RESULT: ${pass} passed, ${fail} failed; evidence: ${OUT}`);
    Deno.exit(fail ? 1 : 0);

The harness spawns fixtures/webmcp-server.ts itself. If that child has already exited — e.g. the port was held and it died on startup — `server.kill()` throws 'Child process has already terminated', which kills the process BEFORE the RESULT line, so an all-green 16/16 run reports exit 1 with no summary. Reproduced on the landed tree: all 16 checks PASS, then the teardown throws and the run exits 1.

Severity: false-red only (a genuine failure is still exit 1), but it is the same family as today's other finds — an exit status that does not describe the checks — and it makes a green harness look broken to anyone re-running it with a fixture already up.

Fix (pushed as fix/cthe-harness-teardown-guard): guard both kills with try/catch. Verified both ways — normal run 16/0 with RESULT and exit 0; run with the fixture pre-started (child dies) 16/0 with RESULT and exit 0, where the unguarded version exited 1 with no RESULT.
